course: dictionary
lesson: 859
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which one the writer means. The word bible is a good example. It can mean a special holy book, a copy of that book, or a book you trust completely.
explain: In RE lessons you read Bible stories, and the capital B shows you mean the big book itself. «The words "a time to be born and a time to die" come from the book of Ecclesiastes in the Bible.» Here the Bible is the book that contains that writing.
explain: Now look at the informal use. Ben says, «This cookbook is my bible.» Ben does not mean a holy book. He means the cookbook is the guide he trusts most. Ask yourself: does the meaning fit the sentence? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A word can have several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: «The Bible» with a capital B means the holy book of Christians, which has the Old Testament and the New Testament.
fact: The Hebrew Bible is the holy book of Jews.
fact: «A bible» with a small b means a copy of the book.
fact: Informally, «my bible» means the most useful and trusted book on a subject, such as a cookbook or a football guide.
exercise: «The words "a time to be born and a time to die" come from the book of Ecclesiastes in the Bible.» Where do these words come from? | *The book of Ecclesiastes in the Bible | A football guide | A cookbook | A time machine
exercise: Ben says, «This cookbook is my bible.» What does bible mean here? | A holy book of Christians | An old book about animals | A copy of the Bible on a shelf | *The most trusted guide on a subject
exercise: In RE lessons pupils learn stories from the Bible. What does Bible mean here? | *The holy book of Christians | A church in a village | A trusted guide to cooking | A copy of a book
test:
Sam keeps a bible on his shelf at home, next to his school books. What does bible most likely mean? | A holy city | A kind of church | *A copy of the holy book | A football fan
Mia says, «Ms Jones's maths book is my bible.» What does she mean? | *The book she trusts most | A holy book of Jews | A cheap, old copy | A book about animals in heaven
exam:
«The family Bible sat on the table at Grandma's house.» What does family Bible most likely mean? | A rule for families to follow | A guide to cooking | *A copy of the Bible kept at home | A holy place in the town
